{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "id": "msg_011Ch1jQXJVcVSEUXkk5dSar", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I'm stopping here. The device and report tools have returned \"BrokenPipeError\" on every call since the SMB dialog, so I can't continue the sweep and I'm not signing off.\n\n**Blocked:** The `device` and `file_report` tools are unreachable. Seven or more calls across observe, screenshot, wait, press_key and open_app all failed the same way. I couldn't file the one open candidate bug, and I haven't confirmed whether the device is still in the SMB dialog.\n\n**Filed:** Nothing yet. My one `file_report` attempt failed with the same broken-pipe error. The developer's earlier reply to the first attempt was \"could not reproduce with the steps given\".\n\n**Open candidate bug (unfiled):** Grid View doesn't survive a rotation. In Amaze > `/storage/emulated/0/AndroidQA/Amaze` in portrait, I chose More options > Grid View and got a grid. After rotating to landscape the folders and files were single-column rows, and the menu showed \"Grid View\" again. Setting Grid View in landscape and rotating back to portrait reverted it the same way. I saw this twice; the developer couldn't reproduce it from the first steps.\n\n**Checked and looked correct:**\n- **Rename:** notes.txt → notes_renamed.txt persisted in the list.\n- **Copy/paste:** keep.jpg and photo.jpg pasted into Beta. The second paste hit a conflict; with \"Do for all items\" + SKIP, both were skipped with no second prompt. With \"Do for all items\" + RENAME, the results were keep (1).jpg and photo (1).jpg, with no second prompt.\n- **Sorting:** Sort by Size descending was correct in both Amaze and Beta, and in Grid View.\n- **Bookmarks:** Alpha was added from the folder menu and appears in the drawer and in Settings > Interface > Bookmarks. In Settings, Alpha → Amaze/Beta and Gamma → Amaze/Alpha were accepted. Alpha → Amaze/Alpha and DCIM → /storage/emulated/0/DCIM were rejected silently, and the list did not change.\n- **SMB dialog:** ticking Anonymous greyed out Username and Password; unticking restored them with the typed value kept.\n\n**Not tested:** Overwrite on paste, the \"Only this folder\" sort option, and actually creating an SMB connection. Also the rename-to-existing-name case, and the Settings > Bookmarks edit and delete flows.\n\n**Next step:** Once the device connection is back, I'd re-file the Grid View report, then finish the untested items before signing off. I haven't saved a memory note because the tools may come back in this session."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 217, "cache_read_input_tokens": 281780, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 217}, "output_tokens": 1, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "efee2b4c-f837-47b3-8205-4c8b679d4540", "uuid": "e4298d7e-1379-4401-a8d7-a1fb02334534", "timestamp": "2026-11-13T22:40:30.690Z", "request_id": "req_011Ch1jQX56ZwqqG1qACnTpX"}
